                <pb facs="0892" n="756" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg756"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/3317: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Culbertson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-03-27T12:00:00-04:00">March 27,
                        1929—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>51. Your 35, March 26, 10 a.m. The Governor of Arica reports that Chilean and
                    Peruvian engineers have examined proposed ports at and north of Escritos; that
                    Chilean engineers made clear that Chile would not under any conditions permit a
                    Peruvian port at the mouth of the River San José; that the engineers
                    representing Peru, <pb facs="0893" n="757" xml:id="pg757"/> who left Arica for
                    Lima this morning, did not indicate the nature of the recommendations which they
                    would make to President Leguia.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
